@startuml

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor black
}

actor "Admin" as User
participant "AdminPage" as UI
participant "AccountController" as Controller
participant "AccountService" as Service
participant "AppUserRepository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB

== UC-07: Manage Customer Accounts ==

User -> UI : 1. Open People & access; edit or lock a customer
activate User
activate UI

UI -> UI : 2. saveCustomerProfile() / updateCustomerStatus()
activate UI
deactivate UI

UI -> UI : 3. Validate form/filter state
activate UI
deactivate UI

UI -> Controller : 4. GET /api/account/users\nPUT /api/account/users/{id}/profile|status
activate Controller

Controller -> Service : 5. users(role) / updateProfile() / updateStatus()
activate Service

Service -> Service : 6. requireAdmin(); prevent self-lock
activate Service
deactivate Service

alt Request is valid and authorized
  Service -> Repo : 7. findAll() / findById(userId)
  activate Repo

  Repo -> DB : 8. SELECT / UPDATE app_user
  activate DB
  DB --> Repo : 9. Customer accounts
  deactivate DB

  Repo --> Service : 10. Repository result
  deactivate Repo

  Service -> Service : 11. Apply profile/status; revoke tokens on status change
  activate Service
  deactivate Service
else Validation, authorization, or state rule fails
  note over Service,Controller
    Non-admin or self-lock -> 403/400
    The service propagates ApiException to ApiExceptionHandler.
  end note
end

Service --> Controller : 12. Domain result or propagated error
deactivate Service

Controller -> Controller : 13. Serialize response
activate Controller
deactivate Controller

Controller --> UI : 14. HTTP 200 or mapped 4xx\nresponse body or error payload
deactivate Controller

UI -> UI : 15. Reload users with refreshAll()
activate UI
deactivate UI

UI --> User : 16. Refresh customer directory and feedback

deactivate UI
deactivate User

@enduml
